{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA supplement — DIRECT evidence the harness ran (not inference)\n\nThe producer's own run ledger survives on disk at\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl`. It records **exactly six tier-2\nruns**, and they bracket the incident:\n\n| run_id | sample_n | finished (UTC) |\n|---|---|---|\n| tier2-current-1a3b33234da9 | 20 | 2026-08-30T23:06:15Z |\n| tier2-current-9d77c4897604 | 20 | 2026-08-31T03:38:48Z |\n| tier2-current-b704c15897fc | 20 | 2026-08-31T05:36:45Z |\n| tier2-diag-single-c399fb26efdb | 1 | 2026-08-31T23:23:38Z |\n| tier2-current-7e13bbcdbac4 | 20 | 2026-09-01T01:00:44Z |\n| tier2-E2-6254dcfde716 | 20 | 2026-09-01T03:36:48Z |\n\nThree independent joins:\n\n1. **Six runs ↔ six observed bursts.** The ticket's own \"6 discrete runs\" is the ledger's\n   run count, not a coincidence of clustering thresholds.\n2. **The last run's finish timestamp is `2026-09-01T03:36:48Z`; the last duplicate in the\n   store is `09-01 03:36`.** Same minute. Nothing ran afterwards, and no duplicate has been\n   created since — which is what the \"105 clean bridge passes\" actually measures.\n3. **`corpus-2026-08-30.manifest.json`** — the replay corpus was built 08-30, the day\n   `tier2.py` landed (`1299d9deb6da`) and the day before the first burst.\n\nEvery artifact in that directory is dated 08-31/09-01 and none has been touched since.\n\n**Honest limit:** the ledger records only *finish* times, so individual CREATE clusters cannot\nbe mapped one-to-one onto individual runs (a 20-sample Opus Pass-1 replay materialises\nper-sample across hours). The run COUNT, the window, and the terminal timestamp all join\nexactly; the per-cluster alignment does not, and is not claimed.\n\n**Invocation path.** `tier2` is a manually invoked CLI subcommand\n(`python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier2 …`, `__main__.py:75`). It is referenced by **no**\nGitHub Actions workflow. That closes the last residual — why it started and why it stopped:\nan operator was iterating on the eval and then stopped. There is no scheduled re-run, so the\nstore has been quiescent since.\n\n## AC7 input (verified independently)\n\nThe existing duplicate probe could not have caught this, for two independent reasons:\n\n- `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets = false` (`rebar.toml:42`, also the code default) — the\n  probe never ran during the burst, so it left no journal and no warning.\n- Even enabled it would have missed: `RECENT_WINDOW_NS = 600 * 1_000_000_000`\n  (`_commands/recent_creates.py:50`) is a **600-second** window, and the measured gap between\n  successive copies of the same title was 19 minutes at the shortest and ~16 hours typically.\n  The probe is designed for a same-session twin filed seconds apart, not a re-run generator.\n\nA detector that would have caught this must be **volume/rate**-based (creation-volume anomaly\nper author/channel per hour) rather than recency-window based, which is what AC7 and\n`prenatal-maudlin-seahorse` (dbe7) call for."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788638823977677001,"uuid":"bbc570b0-104a-4867-8d65-7b8ae1c57798"}